::Q001::[markdown]from:{
	~%-100%παρά + acc#Incorrect. **παρά + acc** means “to the side of” (Chapter 2).
	~%-100%ὑπὸ + gen#Incorrect. **ὑπὸ + gen** means “by (personal agent)” (Chapter 5).
	~%-100%ὑπὸ + acc#Incorrect. **ὑπὸ + acc** means “under (with motion)” (Chapter 5).
	~%-100%περί + gen#Incorrect. **περί + gen** means “concerning” (Chapter 3).
	~%-100%ἄνευ + gen#Incorrect. **ἄνευ + gen** means “without” (Chapter 7).
	~%100%ἀπό + gen#Correct: **ἀπό + gen** → “from” (Chapter 2).
	~%-100%ἐν + dat#Incorrect. **ἐν + dat** means “in” (Chapter 1).
}


::Q002::[markdown]from:{
	~%-100%μετά + acc#Incorrect. **μετά + acc** means “after” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%ὑπὸ + gen#Incorrect. **ὑπὸ + gen** means “by (personal agent)” (Chapter 5).
	~%-100%κατά + gen#Incorrect. **κατά + gen** means “down from” (Chapter 6).
	~%100%ἐκ + gen; ἐξ + gen#Correct: **ἐκ + gen** → “from” (Chapter 1).
	~%-100%εἰς + acc#Incorrect. **εἰς + acc** means “into” (Chapter 1).
	~%-100%παρά + acc#Incorrect. **παρά + acc** means “to the side of” (Chapter 2).
}


::Q003::[markdown]to the side of:{
	~%-100%ἐκ + gen; ἐξ + gen#Incorrect. **ἐκ + gen** means “from” (Chapter 1).
	~%-100%ἀπό + gen#Incorrect. **ἀπό + gen** means “from” (Chapter 2).
	~%-100%πρό + gen#Incorrect. **πρό + gen** means “before” (Chapter 2).
	~%-100%κατά + gen#Incorrect. **κατά + gen** means “down from” (Chapter 6).
	~%-100%ὑπέρ + gen#Incorrect. **ὑπέρ + gen** means “over” (Chapter 9).
	~%100%παρά + acc#Correct: **παρά + acc** → “to the side of” (Chapter 2).
}


::Q004::[markdown]Which Principal Part is the ‘Aorist, Passive, Indicative, 1st person, Singular’?:{
	~%-100%5th#Incorrect. ‘Aorist, Passive, Indicative, 1st person, Singular’ is the **6th Principal Part**, not the 5th.
	~%-100%2nd#Incorrect. ‘Aorist, Passive, Indicative, 1st person, Singular’ is the **6th Principal Part**, not the 2nd.
	~%-100%4th#Incorrect. ‘Aorist, Passive, Indicative, 1st person, Singular’ is the **6th Principal Part**, not the 4th.
	~%-100%3rd#Incorrect. ‘Aorist, Passive, Indicative, 1st person, Singular’ is the **6th Principal Part**, not the 3rd.
	~%100%6th#Correct: ‘Aorist, Passive, Indicative, 1st person, Singular’ is the **6th Principal Part**.
	~%-100%1st#Incorrect. ‘Aorist, Passive, Indicative, 1st person, Singular’ is the **6th Principal Part**, not the 1st.
}


::Q005::[markdown]The **5th Principal Part** is the::{
	~%-100%Perfect, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular#Incorrect. The 5th Principal Part is **Perfect, Middle/Passive, Indicative, 1st person, Singular**, not “Perfect, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular”.
	~%100%Perfect, Middle/Passive, Indicative, 1st person, Singular#Correct: the 5th Principal Part is **Perfect, Middle/Passive, Indicative, 1st person, Singular**.
	~%-100%Aorist, Passive, Indicative, 1st person, Singular#Incorrect. The 5th Principal Part is **Perfect, Middle/Passive, Indicative, 1st person, Singular**, not “Aorist, Passive, Indicative, 1st person, Singular”.
	~%-100%Aorist, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular#Incorrect. The 5th Principal Part is **Perfect, Middle/Passive, Indicative, 1st person, Singular**, not “Aorist, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular”.
	~%-100%Present, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular#Incorrect. The 5th Principal Part is **Perfect, Middle/Passive, Indicative, 1st person, Singular**, not “Present, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular”.
	~%-100%Future, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular#Incorrect. The 5th Principal Part is **Perfect, Middle/Passive, Indicative, 1st person, Singular**, not “Future, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular”.
}


